## 2. HIGH — Architecture & Data Integrity

### 2.1 Duplicate API Endpoints
**Files:**
- `src/app/api/follow-ups/route.ts` AND `src/app/api/followups/route.ts` — two endpoints for the same resource
- `src/app/api/agents/reach/process/[leadId]/route.ts` — Reach agent has its own `withRetry` instead of importing from `@/lib/utils`

**Fix:**
- Remove `follow-ups` (keep `followups` — matches the DB table name)
- Remove duplicate `withRetry` in Reach route, import from `@/lib/utils`

### 2.2 No Input Validation on CRUD Endpoints
**Files:** `src/app/api/leads/route.ts`, `src/app/api/projects/route.ts`, `src/app/api/invoices/route.ts`

POST/PATCH endpoints accept raw JSON bodies and insert directly into Supabase with no validation:
- `POST /api/leads` accepts any fields, no required field checks
- `POST /api/projects` inserts `body` directly without filtering
- `PATCH /api/leads/[id]` spreads `body` into `.update()` — allows overwriting any column including `id`, `created_at`, `campaign_id`

**Fix:**
- Add a validation layer (zod or manual) for each POST/PATCH endpoint
- Whitelist allowed fields for PATCH operations
- Validate types (e.g., `amount_ngn` should be a number)

### 2.3 Scout Agent Has No Error Handling for Tavily API
**File:** `src/app/api/agents/scout/run/route.ts:430-442`

The `tavilySearch` function doesn't check if the response is OK before parsing JSON. If Tavily returns an error, it will crash.

**Fix:**
- Add `if (!res.ok) throw new Error(...)` check
- Add retry logic for 429/5xx responses

### 2.4 HTML Generator Hardcodes Contact Info
**File:** `src/lib/html-generator.ts:977-999`

The generated HTML has hardcoded placeholder phone (`tel:+234`), email (`info@{businessName}.com`), and Instagram (`@businessName`) links. These are fake and will confuse customers.

**Fix:**
- Accept lead contact info as parameters to `generateHTML()`
- Pass actual phone, email, Instagram from the lead record
- If no contact info, omit those sections instead of showing fake placeholders

### 2.5 No Cleanup of `rentnaija` Tables
**Files:** `leadgenAI/supabase/2026-07-20_drop-rentnaija-listings.sql`, `leadgenAI/supabase-migration-008-deploy.sql`

The rentnaija code was removed from the app but the `rentnaija_listings` table may still exist in Supabase. The migration file `008-deploy.sql` references it.

**Fix:**
- Verify the `rentnaija_listings` table is dropped in Supabase
- Remove any remaining references to rentnaija in the codebase

