## 3. MEDIUM — UX & Maintainability

### 3.1 Cookie Consent Doesn't Block Non-Essential Cookies
**File:** `src/components/cookie-consent.tsx`

The cookie consent banner shows and saves preferences, but no code actually checks the preferences before setting analytics/marketing cookies. The `analytics` and `marketing` flags are stored but never read.

**Fix:**
- Create a `useCookieConsent()` hook that checks preferences
- Guard any analytics/marketing scripts behind consent checks
- Add Google Analytics or Plausible integration with consent gating

### 3.2 No Search on Dashboard
**File:** `src/app/dashboard/page.tsx`

The dashboard shows quick stats and recent activity but has no search or filter for leads. Users have to navigate to `/leads` to search.

**Fix:**
- Add a quick search bar on the dashboard
- Add filter dropdowns (category, status)

### 3.3 HTML Generator Lacks Category-Specific Templates
**File:** `src/lib/html-generator.ts`

The generator uses a single template for all categories. A restaurant website looks the same as a salon website. The Dev agent generates different specs per category, but the HTML template doesn't adapt.

**Fix:**
- Add category-specific section layouts (e.g., menu section for restaurants, services grid for salons)
- Add category-specific icons and imagery
- Consider adding a `gallery` section for visual businesses

### 3.4 No Pagination on List Endpoints
**Files:** `src/app/api/leads/route.ts` (has `limit` param but no offset), `src/app/api/campaigns/route.ts`, `src/app/api/projects/route.ts`, `src/app/api/invoices/route.ts`

All list endpoints return all records with no pagination. As the database grows, this will become slow.

**Fix:**
- Add `offset` parameter to all list endpoints
- Add pagination controls on the frontend
- Consider cursor-based pagination for large datasets

### 3.5 Duplicate `withRetry` Implementation
**File:** `src/app/api/agents/reach/process/[leadId]/route.ts:20-30`

Reach agent has its own `withRetry` function instead of importing from `@/lib/utils`. This means retry logic is inconsistent across agents.

**Fix:**
- Remove the local `withRetry` in Reach
- Import from `@/lib/utils`

